title:: Stochastica
summary:: A vocabulary of memory, probability, nonlinear feedback and collective organization
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic, UGens>Generators>Chaotic
related:: Classes/WhiteNoise, Classes/BrownNoise, Classes/LFNoise0, Classes/TIRand, Classes/Stepper

description::
image::scdoc_banner.jpg::

Stochastica supplies raw mathematical models for SuperCollider: deterministic recurrences and flows, shaped independent draws, evolving stochastic trajectories, event timing, discrete state, and collective dynamics. Choose a model for what it remembers and how its parts interact, then make its sonic mapping explicit. A position need not be a pitch; an event intensity need not be a volume; a chaotic coordinate need not fit an audio range.

strong::Deterministic chaos is not stochastic randomness.:: A chaotic map or flow follows its state and parameters without random innovations. Sensitivity to initial conditions can still make its future hard to predict. Stochastic models instead consume probabilistic innovations. Both can sound irregular, but their causes, repeatability and useful controls differ. The documentation's Chaotic>Flows browser category is a technical family, not a claim that every setting or every flow is chaotic.

subsection:: Three rounds of organization

The original collection establishes nonlinear iteration, continuous feedback, independent probability laws, Gaussian drift, fractional approximations, event timing, state transitions, vector covariance and explicit sonification. These are distinct mathematical objects, not interchangeable noise flavors.

Round 2 adds relationships: cross-excitation, inhibition, persistent regimes, material responses to impacts, multivariate motion, metastability, circular geometry and phase synchronization. Round 3 adds derivative-state memory, constrained allocation, accumulated preference, hidden event regimes, stable transport, explicit shocks, opposing populations and spatially extended continuous dynamics. Round 2 and Round 3 are local unreleased expansions in this source tree; publication status does not change their conceptual place in the library.

subsection:: Technical families and complete class inventory

Source folders are implementation organization. The following families describe the mathematical object exposed to a patch. Behavioral roles can cross these families.

